00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:57.762
- Big 4 is made up of
Deloitte, KPMG, EY and PwC.

00:01:57.762 --> 00:02:01.490
And in 2019, they made up over 40%

00:02:01.490 --> 00:02:03.340
of consulting revenue worldwide.

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:05.190
Typically they're much larger than MBB,

00:02:05.190 --> 00:02:07.000
they're more global than MBB,

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:09.370
but they also offer
more services than MBB.

00:02:09.370 --> 00:02:10.750
Over the past few years,

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:13.320
their consulting divisions
have really branched out

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:16.790
to buy smaller agencies, to
do a supply chain consulting,

00:02:16.790 --> 00:02:18.890
innovation consulting, proposition design,

00:02:18.890 --> 00:02:20.640
brand and marketing, and so on.

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:22.450
The other major difference is that MBB

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:25.110
definitely do charge their
clients a little bit more money,

00:02:25.110 --> 00:02:27.580
and that means you're typically
going to get a higher salary

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:29.230
at MBB versus the Big 4.

00:02:29.230 --> 00:02:33.660
- MBB refers to the leading
three strategy consulting firms,

00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:35.900
McKinsey, BCG and Bain.

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:39.100
And strategy consulting
firms is a bit misleading

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:42.870
because these firms do
not only do strategy,

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:45.520
but probably the more
correct term to call them

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:47.670
would be top management consulting.

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:49.720
The vast majority of their business

00:02:49.720 --> 00:02:52.190
is working together
with the top management

00:02:52.190 --> 00:02:55.010
of large clients and trying to help them

00:02:55.010 --> 00:02:57.233
solve the problems and issues

00:02:57.233 --> 00:03:00.470
at the top of mind of the senior leaders

00:03:00.470 --> 00:03:02.560
of the top management of these companies.

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:05.673
Most of these companies
do not officially disclose

00:03:05.673 --> 00:03:09.450
their revenue figures, but
as per the Wikipedia page,

00:03:09.450 --> 00:03:11.790
the latest estimate is that McKinsey

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:14.780
does roughly $10 billion in revenue,

00:03:14.780 --> 00:03:19.620
BCG sits at around 8 billion
and Bain sits around 5 billion.

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:22.380
Regarding employees, McKinsey and BCG

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:25.930
are more or less on a similar
level at around 20,000,

00:03:25.930 --> 00:03:29.980
Whereas Bain sits at about
10,000 employees globally.

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:32.420
My perspective of course will be biased

00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:34.200
by my time at McKinsey

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:36.420
and of course there are also differences

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:37.950
among these three firms.

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:40.760
But overall, also from
talking to friends who worked

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:43.220
at these other companies, at BCG or Bain,

00:03:43.220 --> 00:03:46.550
I do believe that they are
quite similar in many ways,

00:03:46.550 --> 00:03:48.890
which is why you can consider my answers

00:03:48.890 --> 00:03:52.400
indicatively right for
these other firms as well.

00:03:56.150 --> 00:03:58.910
For me personally, it wasn't a big factor.

00:03:58.910 --> 00:04:03.030
I did my undergrad in Munich,
at the university of Munich

00:04:03.030 --> 00:04:06.100
and this is when I applied
to McKinsey for an internship

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:08.760
and while being a good
and renowned university

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:10.300
for business in Germany,

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:14.740
it's a large public university
with thousands of students

00:04:14.740 --> 00:04:17.390
attending the business
program every semester.

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:19.170
But overall, yes, it is true

00:04:19.170 --> 00:04:20.770
that McKinsey likes to hire

00:04:20.770 --> 00:04:22.980
from the so called target schools,

00:04:22.980 --> 00:04:24.800
from these elite universities.

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:27.920
I met lots and lots of people at McKinsey

00:04:27.920 --> 00:04:32.680
who studied at an US Ivy league
or at Oxbridge or at the LSE

00:04:32.680 --> 00:04:35.810
or at any other of these
very renowned universities.

00:04:35.810 --> 00:04:39.100
So for sure this will
increase your chances

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:40.980
of getting into MBB.

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:41.970
And adding to that,

00:04:41.970 --> 00:04:44.300
there might also be
differences in the offices,

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:45.840
how this is perceived.

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:47.180
For instance, in the US,

00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:49.230
the differences among universities

00:04:49.230 --> 00:04:53.040
are much more salient compared
to a country like Germany.

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:55.700
So you can likely expect that in the US,

00:04:55.700 --> 00:04:57.800
the targets schools are more important,

00:04:57.800 --> 00:05:00.020
more relevant than what
they are in Germany.

00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:02.200
So overall, yes, it will help you,

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:05.370
but by no means this
is a hard requirement,

00:05:05.370 --> 00:05:08.110
and you can get successfully into MBB

00:05:08.110 --> 00:05:10.110
without studying at a target school.

00:05:10.110 --> 00:05:12.560
- So I studied at Imperial College London,

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:14.680
and definitely the people
who joined with me,

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:16.290
they definitely came from a variety

00:05:16.290 --> 00:05:17.540
of different universities.

00:05:17.540 --> 00:05:20.640
Honestly, in the past, Big 4
definitely did used to recruit

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:22.980
from these elite schools
that Henry's mentioned

00:05:22.980 --> 00:05:25.450
like Oxbridge, Ivy league and Imperial,

00:05:25.450 --> 00:05:28.250
but diversity is a big
thing for Big 4 firms today

00:05:28.250 --> 00:05:30.660
and they hire from a
variety of universities.

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:33.310
What they've realized is that
hiring from these universities

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:36.060
brings different viewpoints to
the table for their clients.

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:37.470
Everyone has different experiences,

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:39.420
different challenges
and struggles in life,

00:05:39.420 --> 00:05:42.040
and they can go to a variety
of different universities.

00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:43.680
Having a good uni can definitely help you

00:05:43.680 --> 00:05:44.790
get screened, okay?

00:05:44.790 --> 00:05:46.410
But it isn't everything.

00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:49.040
So they look at education, experiences,

00:05:49.040 --> 00:05:51.268
extracurricular activities,
achievements, and skills.

00:05:51.268 --> 00:05:54.280
For anyone thinking that
education plays a massive part

00:05:54.280 --> 00:05:57.660
in the recruitment process, I
would say, go onto LinkedIn,

00:05:57.660 --> 00:06:00.947
have a look at where people
have studied at MBB and Big 4,

00:06:00.947 --> 00:06:03.643
and you'll realize that
education isn't the end all.

00:06:07.490 --> 00:06:09.290
- Yes. Up-or-Out exists.

00:06:09.290 --> 00:06:12.170
And the underlying idea is that over time,

00:06:12.170 --> 00:06:15.326
either you continue
advancing to the next role,

00:06:15.326 --> 00:06:18.389
or at some point, if you fail to advance,

00:06:18.389 --> 00:06:21.760
you will be asked to leave the firm.

00:06:21.760 --> 00:06:25.810
Though it is not as
brutal as it maybe sounds.

00:06:25.810 --> 00:06:28.840
The reason is that
there's a very transparent

00:06:28.840 --> 00:06:32.350
feedback process at every point in time.

00:06:32.350 --> 00:06:35.470
You know where you stand in the process

00:06:35.470 --> 00:06:36.950
and in the evaluation.

00:06:36.950 --> 00:06:39.180
If for any reason, your performance

00:06:39.180 --> 00:06:41.580
would be started to seen as problematic,

00:06:41.580 --> 00:06:44.440
there will be many iterations of feedback

00:06:44.440 --> 00:06:45.790
that people will give you,

00:06:45.790 --> 00:06:48.100
people will actively reach out to you

00:06:48.100 --> 00:06:49.610
to work together with you

00:06:49.610 --> 00:06:51.520
to work on your weak points,

00:06:51.520 --> 00:06:54.030
to make sure that you meet the bar,

00:06:54.030 --> 00:06:57.150
that you meet the requirements
for the next level,

00:06:57.150 --> 00:06:59.280
to really help you as much as possible

00:06:59.280 --> 00:07:01.200
to be successful in the firm.

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:04.510
That being said, at every
level, there will be people

00:07:04.510 --> 00:07:06.860
who will be asked to leave the firm.

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:09.050
If you start at an MBB company,

00:07:09.050 --> 00:07:11.770
you just need to be aware
that these are the rules

00:07:11.770 --> 00:07:13.850
of the game, that this is how it works.

00:07:13.850 --> 00:07:17.100
This being said, if this is
something that happens to you,

00:07:17.100 --> 00:07:19.510
HR professionals will
work together with you

00:07:19.510 --> 00:07:20.960
to find you a new job.

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:23.670
Of course, MBB firms have a vast network

00:07:23.670 --> 00:07:26.800
and will work together with
you to help you identify

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:29.980
new job opportunities
that suit your needs.

00:07:29.980 --> 00:07:32.280
- Yes, in many countries,
Big 4 definitely does have

00:07:32.280 --> 00:07:34.620
an Up-and-Out process, but in the UK,

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:36.760
it's actually very difficult to get fired

00:07:36.760 --> 00:07:38.410
for poor performance.

00:07:38.410 --> 00:07:40.646
We have this Acas code of practice by law.

00:07:40.646 --> 00:07:43.910
It basically says that you
have to consistently show

00:07:43.910 --> 00:07:46.200
you're a bad performer
for a firm to fire you.

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:47.420
They also need to support you,

00:07:47.420 --> 00:07:49.210
so they need to give you a few chances

00:07:49.210 --> 00:07:50.900
and also put you on a supporting plan

00:07:50.900 --> 00:07:53.420
to show that they've tried
to improve your performance.

00:07:53.420 --> 00:07:56.090
So the Big 4 does have very
transparent feedback processes,

00:07:56.090 --> 00:07:58.420
happens once every quarter
where leadership get together

00:07:58.420 --> 00:08:00.910
to speak about you, to
understand who needs support,

00:08:00.910 --> 00:08:02.850
and identify how everyone's doing.

00:08:02.850 --> 00:08:05.270
That means there's also a very
structured promotion process.

00:08:05.270 --> 00:08:07.430
So once every year in the junior levels,

00:08:07.430 --> 00:08:09.910
you can go for promotion,
even early promotion,

00:08:09.910 --> 00:08:11.500
and you have a defined set of guidelines

00:08:11.500 --> 00:08:15.140
that you need to meet every
grade for you to get promoted.

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:17.430
So it's really clear if you
want to go for promotion,

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:19.563
you know exactly what you need to do.

00:08:23.460 --> 00:08:25.180
- Regarding the project set up,

00:08:25.180 --> 00:08:28.830
what probably distinguishes
most MBB projects

00:08:28.830 --> 00:08:31.910
from Big 4 projects is the team size

00:08:31.910 --> 00:08:35.320
and the type of topics that
the consultants will work on.

00:08:35.320 --> 00:08:39.540
It is no secret that MBB
fees are rather expensive.

00:08:39.540 --> 00:08:43.000
And for sure, more expensive
than your average Big 4 firm.

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:46.000
For these reasons, MBB
teams are rather small

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:48.250
and rather work on the most important,

00:08:48.250 --> 00:08:51.590
most pressing challenges
that the company is facing.

00:08:51.590 --> 00:08:56.110
A typical MBB team size ranges
from two to four consultants,

00:08:56.110 --> 00:08:57.940
including the project lead,

00:08:57.940 --> 00:09:00.930
and then one or two
partners joining the team

00:09:00.930 --> 00:09:02.320
once or twice a week,

00:09:02.320 --> 00:09:04.960
and then adding their value
and their perspective as well.

00:09:04.960 --> 00:09:08.140
This means that from early
on, you are one of two,

00:09:08.140 --> 00:09:10.810
one of three or one of four consultants.

00:09:10.810 --> 00:09:12.014
And of course by that,

00:09:12.014 --> 00:09:14.920
you are a significant part of the team.

00:09:14.920 --> 00:09:17.740
The responsibility that
you will get early on

00:09:17.740 --> 00:09:21.550
from your very first
project will be significant.

00:09:21.550 --> 00:09:23.690
Due to the importance of the topics

00:09:23.690 --> 00:09:25.540
that MBB firms work with,

00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:28.330
you will work together with
rather senior executives,

00:09:28.330 --> 00:09:30.500
often even with board members,

00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:33.530
and will learn to develop
documents for this audience

00:09:33.530 --> 00:09:35.640
and present in front of them as well.

00:09:35.640 --> 00:09:38.630
This being said, MBB
firms in the last years,

00:09:38.630 --> 00:09:41.832
tried to expand the
diversity of the projects

00:09:41.832 --> 00:09:43.700
in other directions as well,

00:09:43.700 --> 00:09:47.570
which is why today you can
find projects in an MBB firm

00:09:47.570 --> 00:09:50.130
that now more closely resemble projects

00:09:50.130 --> 00:09:51.920
that you would also find in Big 4.

00:09:51.920 --> 00:09:54.470
Specifically, most MBB firms today

00:09:54.470 --> 00:09:57.900
also have different variations
of implementation type

00:09:57.900 --> 00:09:59.290
of inciting services.

00:09:59.290 --> 00:10:03.460
This means that you do not
only work on super strategic,

00:10:03.460 --> 00:10:05.005
super conceptual projects,

00:10:05.005 --> 00:10:07.500
but you also might find
yourself in a position

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:09.970
to really work on projects
that are much closer

00:10:09.970 --> 00:10:11.550
to implementation setting

00:10:11.550 --> 00:10:13.200
that are really about execution

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:14.690
and bringing ideas to life.

00:10:14.690 --> 00:10:17.168
Often ideas that then
prior teams before you

00:10:17.168 --> 00:10:19.050
develop with the client.

00:10:19.050 --> 00:10:21.930
So from this perspective
there for sure is an overlap

00:10:21.930 --> 00:10:23.820
regarding the types of projects

00:10:23.820 --> 00:10:26.680
and the team set up between MBB and Big 4.

00:10:26.680 --> 00:10:29.160
Though still, the typical MBB project

00:10:29.160 --> 00:10:32.180
will be different than
the typical Big 4 project.

00:10:32.180 --> 00:10:33.440
- Just like Henry's mentioned,

00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:36.167
MBB have definitely branched
out to the implementation work

00:10:36.167 --> 00:10:37.960
but Big 4 definitely rule king

00:10:37.960 --> 00:10:39.830
when it comes to breadth of services.

00:10:39.830 --> 00:10:41.480
We acquired some really cool companies

00:10:41.480 --> 00:10:43.840
to strengthen our practices from strategy,

00:10:43.840 --> 00:10:45.520
technology, operations,

00:10:45.520 --> 00:10:47.570
supply chain, human capital,

00:10:47.570 --> 00:10:50.020
as well as brand,
marketing and innovation.

00:10:50.020 --> 00:10:52.110
If you're working on a
strategy or prime project,

00:10:52.110 --> 00:10:55.030
you typically do work in
small teams of two to four.

00:10:55.030 --> 00:10:56.850
You'll end up having a partner

00:10:56.850 --> 00:10:58.950
who looks after the
relationship with the client,

00:10:58.950 --> 00:11:00.590
a manager, and maybe an analyst

00:11:00.590 --> 00:11:02.230
or consultant on that team.

00:11:02.230 --> 00:11:03.990
On operations or technology projects,

00:11:03.990 --> 00:11:06.970
they can be really
small, from two to four,

00:11:06.970 --> 00:11:09.690
but they can be massive to 300.

00:11:09.690 --> 00:11:12.628
So you need to have a variety
of leadership on there

00:11:12.628 --> 00:11:14.395
and work in smaller structures

00:11:14.395 --> 00:11:17.100
whereas still ensuring there's a big team.

00:11:17.100 --> 00:11:19.460
So typically they end
up being in work streams

00:11:19.460 --> 00:11:20.970
and you have smaller teams within it,

00:11:20.970 --> 00:11:23.240
but those small teams end
up being from four to 15

00:11:23.240 --> 00:11:24.660
to even 20 sometimes.

00:11:24.660 --> 00:11:25.560
- Thank you for watching.

00:11:25.560 --> 00:11:28.500
